  "aiContextParagraph": "Following a formal mandate from President Isaac Herzog, opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has begun the process of forming a new government in Israel. Eisenkot, the leader of the Yashar party and a former military chief, has up to six weeks to navigate the country’s complex political landscape to secure a parliamentary majority. During his initial efforts, he has expressed openness to engaging with various political factions, including allies of former Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Eisenkot has stated that the country faces a historic crisis and is nearing a critical juncture. International and local media report that while alliances with Arab Israeli parties present a mathematical path to power, such coalitions remain politically sensitive. The outcome of these negotiations remains uncertain, with analysts considering various scenarios should Eisenkot fail to reach the required agreements within the designated timeframe.",
